% This is a placeholder for the Stateflow chart implementation.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would be a graphical Stateflow file
% implementing the adaptive excitation control logic.

% States:
% - IDLE: Waiting for start signal
% - EXCITE: Applying excitation pulse
% - ESTIMATE: Estimating ECM parameters from response
% - EVALUATE_UNCERTAINTY: Checking if parameter estimates have converged
% - CONVERGED: Parameters have converged, optionally hold or reduce rate
% - NOT_CONVERGED: Parameters not converged, increase amplitude/rate (within safety limits)

% Transitions:
% IDLE -> EXCITE: Start signal received
% EXCITE -> ESTIMATE: Excitation pulse completed
% ESTIMATE -> EVALUATE_UNCERTAINTY: Parameter estimation completed
% EVALUATE_UNCERTAINTY -> CONVERGED: Uncertainty below threshold
% EVALUATE_UNCERTAINTY -> NOT_CONVERGED: Uncertainty above threshold
% CONVERGED -> IDLE: Hold time elapsed or new cycle requested
% NOT_CONVERGED -> EXCITE: Increase amplitude/rate and try again (with safety limits)

% The chart would output:
% - excitation_amplitude: Amplitude for next pulse
% - excitation_width: Width for next pulse
% - excitation_period: Period for next pulse
% - reset_estimator: Signal to reset parameter estimator
% - hold_control: Signal to hold or reduce excitation rate

% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Stateflow editor to create the graphical state machine.